      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "Find ${f}^{′}(x)$ for $f(x)={11}^{x}-5\\operatorname{ln}⁡x.$",
      "worked_solution": "Taking the derivative, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({11}^{x}-5\\operatorname{ln}⁡x) \\\\  & ={11}^{x}\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}⁡11-5(\\frac{1}{x}) \\\\  & ={11}^{x}\\operatorname{ln}⁡11-\\frac{5}{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
