      "name": "Question 6",
      "problem": "Calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ for $y=-5{e}^{x}+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x.$",
      "worked_solution": "Taking the derivative, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-5{e}^{x}+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x) \\\\  & =-5{e}^{x}+2(\\frac{1}{x}) \\\\  & =-5{e}^{x}+\\frac{2}{x}.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
