    "q-339994": {
      "dom_id": "step-q339994",
      "name": "Question 8",
      "problem": "Given the function $y=2{x}^{3}+x-3{log}_{6}⁡x,$ find the instantaneous rate of change at $x=3.$ Do not round the answer.\n\nThe instantaneous rate of change at $x=3$ is\n{{field-1}}.",
      "worked_solution": "To differentiate a logarithm with base $a,$ we use the formula\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({log}_{a}⁡x)=\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡a}.\n$$\n\nTo find the instantaneous rate of change at a given point, we have to find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ at that point.\n\nTaking the derivative we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2{x}^{3}+x-3{log}_{6}⁡x) \\\\  & =2\\cdot 3{x}^{2}+1-3\\cdot \\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡6} \\\\  & =6{x}^{2}+1-\\frac{3}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the instantaneous rate of change at $x=3$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=3} & ={(6{x}^{2}+1-\\frac{3}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡6})|}_{x=3} \\\\  & =6(3)^{2}+1-\\frac{3}{3\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}⁡6} \\\\  & =55-\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡6}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
