    "q-17369": {
      "dom_id": "step-q17369",
      "name": "Question 10",
      "problem": "Given that $y=2x-5\\operatorname{ln}⁡x$,  find the slope of the tangent at $x=1.$",
      "worked_solution": "To find the slope of the tangent at a given point, we have to find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ at that point.\n\nTaking the derivative, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2x-5\\operatorname{ln}⁡x) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2x)-5\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x) \\\\  & =2-5\\cdot \\frac{1}{x} \\\\  & =2-\\frac{5}{x}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the tangent at $x=1$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=1} & ={(2-\\frac{5}{x})|}_{x=1} \\\\  & =2-\\frac{5}{1} \\\\  & =2-5 \\\\  & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
